Rule 10 (there exists a valid index along the reduction axis)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_2 else v_2 + ndim(v_1)) > 0 ∧ ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_2 else v_2 + ndim(v_1)) - 1] : i ≥ 0 ∧ i ≤ shape(v_1, if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_2 else v_2 + ndim(v_1)) - 1
>>
Rule 12 (valid axis values for 2-D input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then (v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = -1 ∨ v_2 = -2)
